{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory delivered strong immediate safety management: red-flag screening, urgent-return thresholds, licorine dosing, no self-injection, hematology follow-up, repeat CBC timing, and caregiver teach-back were all made executable. However, there were minor responsibility-chain omissions: medication reconciliation did not visibly verify chronic/psychiatric medicines, the record plan did not include the case-specific outside chemotherapy/intrathecal/bone-marrow/imaging records, and the psychiatric/non-cooperation barrier was not converted into a privacy-preserving disclosure plan for the treating team. Under the rubric, any minor responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite high-order strengths.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00286",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave an executable home checklist after the CBC and onsite hematology review.",
        "quote": "回家清单"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00300",
        "explanation": "The caregiver demonstrated receipt of the key medication, emergency, and repeat-CBC plan.",
        "quote": "我理解的是三件事"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The bounded episode closed with the patient afebrile and monitored, licorine use and no self-injection clarified, urgent red flags specified, and repeat hematology/CBC follow-up planned. Residual omissions around psychiatric disclosure and complete outside-record preparation make the overall trajectory borderline, but the immediate home transition itself was traceable and executable.",
